Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||02-03-2001||08:03 AM||||on my 86SE,2.8L, I jusy installed this motor outta my totalled GT....  Is the place for the temp gauge on the *bottom* intake near the pulley side pointong upward? This is my ??,   There was not an extra wire on the wiring harness to plug in there?? there was nothing on the ORIGINAL 2.8L that was in the SE!! How can I finf out where the damn wire is for the temp. sensor?? any help very much appreciatted(sp.lol) <P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Luperman||02-03-2001||10:05 AM||||the temp gauge sensor is located right above the exhaust manifold facing the trunk<P>------------------<BR>86 fiero SE 2M6        84 Grand Wagoneer 360||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||02-03-2001||11:08 AM||||There are 3 temp sensors/senders on the V6 <BR>1 for the gage and idiot light ( in the head by the dist).<BR>1 for the fan (1 wire by the thermo housing)<BR>1 for the ECM (2 wire by the thermo housing)<BR>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||02-03-2001||11:18 AM||||ok... I think...  lol<BR>Does it have two wire connecter's?? &lt;-- That's the one I mean that's faces the trunk by the dist. !  OK Then what is the thing on the lower intake facing upward with a round connecter??  I can't even find an extra wire on the harness for this thing?? <BR>Another ?? Where is the Oil Pressure connecter located on the motor??<BR>Thank's again for the advice!!!<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||02-03-2001||01:08 PM||||The one in the head by the dist. is 2 wire. To check turn on ign. and ground the wires - the light should light and the gage should peg. The oil pressure sender(3 wire) is on the end of a metal pipe that terminates under the batt. area||||reg||1
